==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|luke|lang=enm}}, {{term|leuke|lang=enm}}, {{term|lewke||lukewarm, tepid|lang=enm}}, from an unexplained variant or extension of {{etyl|enm}} {{term|lewe||warm, lukewarm, tepid|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|hleow|hlēow|warm|lang=ang}}, perhaps due to confusion with {{etyl|ang}} {{term|wlæc||tepid, lukewarm, cool|lang=ang}}.

